course: dictionary
lesson: 10493
title: A turtle is a reptile
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A turtle is a reptile with a hard shell on its back that covers its body. The clue is in the list: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Turtles are grouped with snakes and lizards, so a turtle is a reptile, not an amphibian.
explain: The shell is the turtle's home and its armour. «The jaguar has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat and can crack turtle shells.» A shell that a jaguar's bite can crack is hard, but it is still the turtle's protection.
explain: Turn turtle is a phrase that means turn upside down. Many turtles live in the sea, and sea turtles can swim thousands of kilometres. In American English, turtle can also mean any animal with this kind of shell, including tortoises. Check the context to see which meaning fits.
fact: A turtle is a reptile with a hard shell on its back that covers its body.
fact: Turtles are cold-blooded, breathe air and lay their eggs on land.
fact: Sea turtles can swim thousands of kilometres.
fact: In American English, turtle can mean any animal with this kind of shell, including tortoises.
fact: «Turn turtle» means turn upside down.
exercise: «The jaguar can crack turtle shells.» What is a turtle shell? | The turtle's tail | A kind of seaweed | *The hard covering that protects a turtle's body | A soft pouch for eggs
exercise: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Which of these is a reptile? | *Turtles | Frogs | Salamanders | Toads
exercise: «Green turtles visit cleaning stations where fish pick algae off their shells.» Find and copy one word that means the hard coverings on turtles. | visit | cleaning | fish | *shells
test: Are turtles reptiles or amphibians, according to the list in the context? | Newts | Frogs | *Reptiles | Amphibians
test: In American English, what can turtle mean? | Only animals that live in ponds | *Any animal with this kind of shell, including tortoises | Only sea animals | A bird with a long beak
exam: Why are plastic bags dangerous for sea turtles? | Turtles can only swim in clear water | Turtles use them to build nests | Plastic bags are too heavy for turtles to lift | *Plastic bags look like jellyfish, which turtles may eat
